WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.580
He planted a willow sapling in a measured pot of soil and watered it for five years.

2
00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:10.603
The tree gained 164 pounds.

3
00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:12.343
The soil lost 2 ounces.

4
00:00:12.843 --> 00:00:14.103
Where had the mass come from?

5
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:19.567
Not the dirt, which had barely moved from water, and from something in the air he

6
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.547
could not see, weigh, or hold.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.770
That same instinct, that the invisible could be real if it left a measurable mark,

8
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.970
led him to the vapor that boils off fermenting wine, and for it he coined a word

9
00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:37.770
from the Greek chaos: "For want of a name, I have called that vapour Gas, being not

10
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.930
far severed from the chaos of the ancients."

11
00:00:40.733 --> 00:00:44.073
The willow experiment is the whole of biochemistry and miniature.

12
00:00:44.493 --> 00:00:49.673
A living thing grows; trust the balance, not the story; if the invisible leaves a

13
00:00:49.673 --> 00:00:51.453
mark you can measure, it is real.

14
00:00:52.013 --> 00:00:54.173
The chapter you are starting rests on that bet.
